mod:store_rootless_destination_prices;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b8, row 2: the rootless destination's other roads, S1bA). THE ROW'S PRICES (rulings l.13248 item 2): right programs main
// runs to 67 that the row refuses, failing closed, each marked PRICE and pinned by its site, followed by its TWIN, which main (3159ab8) refuses at
// the same site. They're one kind: the new arms write the target whole into the store's records or the callee's summary, so a view of another part of
// the target is refused across it. AT PARITY, 14: S1's `rw_ls_ok`; the attack on S1's five (`gen_ow`, `pk_ok`, `pr_loop`, `pr_ow`, `pr_pv`); `pk2`'s
// three, DEF-633's BORROW-009 at a `pick` binding (`pk2_c_ok`, `pk2_dd_ok`, `pk2_ok`); and `j2`'s five (`j2_pw_ok`, `j2_pww_ok`, `j2_ssl_ok`,
// `j2_sslw_ok`, `j2_sub3_c`). Most twins name the selection through a pointer local; `pk_ok`'s and the `pr_` twins make the store by the target's
// name. `pk2_c_okt` is made for this row by the cells' rule, the store spelled through a pointer local `t`. The `j2` cells' `_nm` forms, a plain
// store through one target only, drop the second target, so they aren't twins (l.13248); they run 67 on main and here, in
// tests/backend/programs/store_rootless_destination_faces_ok.npk. The faces are in store_rootless_destination_faces.npk. PINNED, refused by main and
// here at the same site, for the row's mutants: `rw_mx_c`, a pointer parameter's target beside a local's address under one ternary, whose refs go
// into the pointer's value alone (`onp`).
error:E5;
// PRICE: `gen_ow`, a right program main runs to 67, refused here at its store (one site); at parity. Its twin `gen_ow_tw` follows.
// Ailp-team_156, item 2 price, a GENERIC `T`: pr_ow in a generic function: the stored `.ptr` overwritten by `zc` before `h.p` is freed. Right.
struct:Bx_gen_ow<T> = { T:v; wild any->:p; };
func:gs_gen_ow<T> = int64(move T:x, move T:y, int64:n) {
    string:s = string_concat("ab", "cde");
    wild int8->:zb = alloc(8i64);
    wild int8->:zc = alloc(8i64);
    Bx_gen_ow<T>:h = Bx_gen_ow{ v: move(x), p: zb =>! wild any-> };
    Bx_gen_ow<T>:h2 = Bx_gen_ow{ v: move(y), p: zb =>! wild any-> };
    (<-(is (n > 100i64) : @h2 : @h)).p = s.ptr =>! wild any->;
    h.p = zc =>! wild any->;
    dalloc(h.p);
    dalloc(zb);
    pass 7i64;
};
func:cell_main_gen_ow = int32() never fails { pass (((gs_gen_ow::<int64>(1i64, 2i64, 1i64) ?! E5) + 60i64) =>! int32); };
// TWIN: `gen_ow_tw`, the ternary named through a pointer local `t`: main refuses it at the same site.
// Ailp-team_156, gen_ow BY-NAME TWIN, a GENERIC `T`: pr_ow in a generic function: the stored `.ptr` overwritten by `zc` before `h.p` is freed. Right.
struct:Bx_gen_ow_tw<T> = { T:v; wild any->:p; };
func:gs_gen_ow_tw<T> = int64(move T:x, move T:y, int64:n) {
    string:s = string_concat("ab", "cde");
    wild int8->:zb = alloc(8i64);
    wild int8->:zc = alloc(8i64);
    Bx_gen_ow_tw<T>:h = Bx_gen_ow_tw{ v: move(x), p: zb =>! wild any-> };
    Bx_gen_ow_tw<T>:h2 = Bx_gen_ow_tw{ v: move(y), p: zb =>! wild any-> };
    Bx_gen_ow_tw<T>->:t = is (n > 100i64) : @h2 : @h; (<-t).p = s.ptr =>! wild any->;
    h.p = zc =>! wild any->;
    dalloc(h.p);
    dalloc(zb);
    pass 7i64;
};
func:cell_main_gen_ow_tw = int32() never fails { pass (((gs_gen_ow_tw::<int64>(1i64, 2i64, 1i64) ?! E5) + 60i64) =>! int32); };
